Before Starting Kali Linux check network adapter(It is at left side below Power-on in Devices). It should be NAT or Bridged.

Step 1: Start kali Linux in Vmware.
Step 2: Run sudo wireshark in terminal or direct open wireshark
Step 3: Select Active Interface and double click on it(e.g., eth0)
Step 4: To Start capture click on blue shark pin icon, then network packets begin appearing 
Step 5: Generate traffic using browser in https://www.google.com or ping google.com in terminal.
Step 6: Apply filters like icmp, dns, tcp
Step 7: Inspect packet details 
Step 8: Check TCP Stream
>>commands:
$ curl http://example.com
$ curl http://google.com
Right click on TCP Packet > Follow - TCP Stream
Step 9: Click on File > save as .pcapng. > To Stop capture CTRL+C
Step 10: Analyze Statistics
